Package: researchR
Title: Client for a Self-Hosted 'researchd' Literature Surveillance Server
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-08-26
Authors@R: person("Raban", "Heller",
 email = "raban.heller@uni-ulm.de",
 role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"),
 comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-8006-9742"))
Description: An R client for 'researchd', the self-hosted literature and
 signal surveillance server it is built for. 'researchd'
 watches PubMed, Europe PMC, OpenAlex, Crossref, Semantic Scholar,
 ClinicalTrials.gov and the preprint servers on a schedule, deduplicates
 and classifies what it finds by study type, and tracks non-publication
 signals such as trial registrations, regulatory decisions and filings.
 This package talks to its token-authenticated REST API, returning
 questions, records and signals as tidy 'tibble' objects, and lets you
 create and edit the surveillance questions themselves from R rather
 than from the browser dashboard.
